    "apiVersion": "VERSION_0",
    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Simulates three-point estimates and risk events to give P10 / P50 / P80 / P90 totals, contingency, the probability of exceeding a budget, and the drivers of uncertainty.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Finance",
    "tags": [
        "Monte Carlo",
        "cost risk",
        "simulation",
        "PERT",
        "contingency",
        "risk register",
        "P80",
        "project estimate",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Turns **three-point estimates** (low, most likely, high) for each line of a project estimate, budget, bid or forecast into a probability distribution of the total, by Monte Carlo simulation.\n\n- Each line is sampled from a **PERT** (default), triangular or uniform distribution\n- **Risk events** from a risk register occur with their probability (0-1 or %); lines with no probability always occur\n- Optional **correlation** between lines (a single rank correlation, applied with the Iman-Conover method): treating lines as independent usually understates the risk\n- **P10, P50, P80, P90, P95** of the total and of each group, the **contingency** needed above the base estimate for each confidence level, and the chance of exceeding the base or a target\n- **Drivers**: which lines contribute most to the uncertainty (share of variance and rank correlation with the total), for a tornado chart\n- The **S-curve** of the total (histogram with cumulative probability)\n\nThe base estimate is the sum of the most likely values of the lines that always occur. A fixed random seed makes runs repeatable.",
    "dependencies": "",
